WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:04.120
Welcome back to Second Drink of Fun Run Part 2.
欢迎回到《趣味长跑》第二部分节目的第二杯。

2
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.720
I mentioned this last week.
我上周提过这个。

3
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.420
I love these episodes so much.
我太喜欢这些单集了。

4
00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.900
I had such a blast filming my scenes for Fun Run.
我拍《趣味长跑》的戏份时玩得太开心了。

5
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.600
Well, we got to get out of the office.
嗯，我们终于能离开办公室了。

6
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:13.140
We always enjoyed sunshine.
我们总是很喜欢阳光。

7
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.560
We talk about that.
我们聊过这个。

8
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.000
I really love the pictures from this episode.
我真的很喜欢这一集的照片。

9
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.500
I have so many.
我有好多。

10
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.500
We brought our cameras, but also NBC sent photographers out
我们带了相机，但NBC也派了摄影师去，

11
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.260
and they got a ton of behind-the-scenes moments.
他们拍了大量幕后花絮照片。

12
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.240
They're still on the NBC website.
它们现在还在NBC官网上。

13
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.440
I saw one of Greg talking through a scene
我看到一张格雷格在跟我和约翰

14
00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:32.320
with me and John.
对戏的照片。

15
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.020
And Angela, there's such a sweet one of you and Steve
安吉拉，有一张你和史蒂夫的照片特别温馨，

16
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.260
just walking and talking.
你们俩边走边聊。

17
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.860
It just, it really made me miss us.
这真的，真的让我怀念我们在一起的日子。

18
00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:43.640
Yeah, I miss our little hangouts between scenes,
是啊，我很想念我们在片场休息时的小聚，

19
00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.680
especially when we're on location.
特别是当我们去外景地的时候。

20
00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.640
And this was especially fun
而且这次格外有趣，

21
00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.400
because we were coming back from a summer break,
因为我们刚结束暑假回来，

22
00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.780
so we were all real chatty.
所以大家都有说有笑的。

23
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.160
Yeah, well, we can't talk about Fun Run
对啊，我们聊《趣味长跑》

24
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.740
and not discuss Sprinkles.
就不能不提小饼干。

25
00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:56.140
R.I.P.
安息吧。

26
00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:56.560
Sprinkles.
小饼干。

27
00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:56.920
Yes.
是的。

28
00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:58.960
And you know, we got a lot of mail
你知道的，我们收到了很多邮件，

29
00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.320
about whose fault it really was for Sprinkles' death.
都在讨论小饼干的死到底该怪谁。

30
00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.960
We discussed this in our episode
我们在那期专讲安吉拉·马丁的单集里

31
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.080
all about Angela Martin.
讨论过这件事。

32
00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:07.040
We had said maybe if Pam hadn't made Angela
我们曾说过，要不是帕姆非要让安吉拉

33
00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.620
go to the hospital in the first place to see Meredith,
去医院看梅雷迪思，

34
00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:11.620
that Sprinkles would still be alive.
小饼干说不定现在还活着呢。

35
00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.220
But Angie Z wrote in and said this,
但安吉·Z来信写道：

36
00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:17.660
I don't think Pam was responsible for Sprinkles' death.
我不认为帕姆应该为小饼干的死负责。

37
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.940
It was definitely Dwight's fault.
这绝对是德怀特的错。

38
00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.660
You can clearly see how much he doesn't care
你分明能看出他有多不在乎

39
00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:25.620
about doing the tasks that Angela asked him to do for her cat.
去完成安吉拉交代给他的关于她猫咪的任务。

40
00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:27.300
He probably didn't do it right
他很可能根本没做好，

41
00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.900
because he wasn't even paying attention
因为当安吉拉告诉他怎么给小饼干喂药时，

42
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:31.580
when she was telling him how to give Sprinkles her medicine.
他根本就没在听。

43
00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.420
Most definitely Dwight's fault.
绝对是德怀特的错。

44
00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:35.800
I appreciate it.
我很感激。

45
00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:36.640
I do.
我是认真的。

46
00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.600
I really took on, as Pam,
作为帕姆，我在听了

47
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:39.900
some of that responsibility
我们那期《走近安吉拉·马丁》之后，

48
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:42.080
after our All About Angela Martin episode.
确实把一部分责任揽到了自己身上。

49
00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:43.900
Well, it is true.
嗯，确实如此。

50
00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.900
I mean, she gave Dwight a whole written-out liSt.
我是说，她给德怀特列了一整张写得满满的清单。

51
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.360
All he had to do was look at it.
他只需要看一眼就行了。

52
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:48.980
Exactly.
没错。

53
00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:50.540
Well, in this breakdown,
嗯，在这个细节剖析中，

54
00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:52.920
we also talk about how the documentary crew
我们还谈到了纪录片摄制组

55
00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.040
pulled Jim and Pam into the conference room
是如何把吉姆和帕姆拉进会议室的，

56
00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.760
to show them footage that proves they're dating.
为了给他们看证明他们正在交往的素材。

57
00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:00.160
And it got us wondering,
这让我们不禁好奇，

58
00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.580
why is the documentary crew getting involved
为什么摄制组会插手，

59
00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:06.080
when there's so many examples of them not getting involved?
明明有那么多他们没有插手的例子？

60
00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.060
Well, Ashley S.
嗯，阿什利·S

61
00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:10.180
had a theory that I thought was interesting.
有一个观点我觉得很有意思。

62
00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:11.280
Ashley says,
阿什利说，

63
00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.540
I figured out why the crew intervened
我弄清楚了为什么摄制组会介入

64
00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:16.480
to force a romantic admission out of Jim and Pam
强迫吉姆和帕姆承认恋情，

65
00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:20.160
while previously leaving Andy to float away at the lake.
而之前却任由安迪在湖上漂走。

66
00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.300
Guys, it is so obvious.
伙计们，这太明显了。

67
00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:25.880
They are asking to get the scoop for their boy, Brian.
他们是为了给他们的好兄弟布赖恩套出猛料。

68
00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.400
Oh, yes.
哦，是的。

69
00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:29.660
Do you think?
你觉得呢？

70
00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.160
I mean...
我是说……

71
00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:33.640
At this point, though, aren't they couples friends?
不过话说回来，此时他们难道不是情侣朋友吗？

72
00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.740
No, because Jim and Pam aren't, like, a couple yet, so...
不对，因为吉姆和帕姆还没在一起，所以……

73
00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.020
They're not a couple yet, and Pam is single.
他们还没在一起，而且帕姆还是单身。

74
00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.640
I guess, but isn't Brian married?
我猜是吧，但布赖恩不是结婚了吗？

75
00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:45.060
We don't know when Brian got married, I guess.
我想我们不知道布赖恩是什么时候结婚的。

76
00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:45.780
We don't know.
我们不知道。

77
00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:46.640
Hmm, okay.
嗯，好吧。

78
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.140
I mean, Ashley, I think it's a fun theory.
我是说，阿什利，我觉得这是个有趣的观点。

79
00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.340
It's kind of a stir-in-the-pot kind of theory.
这算是一种唯恐天下不乱的观点。

80
00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:52.160
It really is.
确实如此。

81
00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:56.000
All right, well, I wanted to address this question from Anna M.
好吧，我想回答安娜·M提出的这个问题。

82
00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.200
Anna says,
安娜说，

83
00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:00.500
Why wasn't Angela's funeral lady in mourning garb
为什么安吉拉的葬礼女郎的丧服

84
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.320
mentioned as part of the wardrobe breakdown?
没有被提及作为服装剖析的一部分？

85
00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.960
It seems like the perfect missed opportunity.
这似乎是一个完美的错失良机。

86
00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:05.700
Hmm.
嗯。

87
00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.320
Anna, you're so right.
安娜，你太对了。

88
00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.960
I can't believe I missed that costume breakdown,
我真不敢相信我漏掉了那个服装剖析，

89
00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:10.920
so here you go.
所以给你补上。

90
00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:15.600
Angela's mourning outfit consists of a black, silky camisole
安吉拉的丧服包括一件黑色的丝质吊带衫，

91
00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:19.020
covered with a sheer black lace long-sleeved blouse
外面罩着一件黑色薄纱长袖衬衫，

92
00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.020
with black piping.
带有黑色滚边。

93
00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.800
It has a scrunched high collar
它有一个褶皱的高领，

94
00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:25.700
and lots of tiny black buttons down the front,
正面有许多密集的黑色小纽扣，

95
00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:29.320
and the sleeves have this kind of scrunched poof at the end
袖子末端有一种褶皱泡泡袖的设计，

96
00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:30.780
like a poet's blouse.
就像诗人的衬衫一样。

97
00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.980
Pair that with a black skirt and an updo,
搭配一条黑色短裙和一个盘发，

98
00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.400
and there you have Angela's mourning outfit.
安吉拉的丧服就是这样了。

99
00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:38.080
Such great detail by our costume department.
我们的服装部门处理的细节真是太棒了。

100
00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:38.760
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

101
00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:40.820
Well, one last thing.
好吧，还有最后一件事。

102
00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.480
I wanted to share this deleted Michael talking head
我想分享这段被删掉的迈克尔单人访谈片段

103
00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:47.760
because we're going to find out what famous philanthropist
因为我们要来看看，迈克尔说他长得像

104
00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.480
Michael says he looks like.
哪位著名的慈善家。

105
00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:50.540
This is really funny.
这个真的很好笑。

106
00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:55.660
Yeah, the charity is having some financial probleMs.
对，慈善机构遇到了一些财务问题。

107
00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.560
What do I look like to you, Paul Newman?
你在我身上看到了谁的影子，保罗·纽曼吗？

108
00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.500
That's actually not a good example
其实这并不是个好例子

109
00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:06.140
because I have been compared to a young Paul Newman,
因为我曾被比作年轻时的保罗·纽曼

110
00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:07.440
my eyes and my face,
我的眼睛和我的脸

111
00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:10.080
and I make my own salad dressing.
而且我自己调配沙拉酱。

112
00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:13.300
I mix Newman's ranch with Newman's Italian,
我把纽曼的田园沙拉酱和纽曼的意式沙拉酱混合在一起

113
00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:16.140
sell it at flea markets for a slight loss.
拿到跳蚤市场去卖，稍微有点亏本。

114
00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:20.820
I could make a profit if I changed one of the ingredients
如果我把其中一种配料

115
00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.200
to wishbone, but I won't do it.
换成威士邦，我本可以盈利，但我不会这么做。

116
00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:23.800
Yeah.
对。

117
00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:25.900
Yeah, he looks like Paul Newman.
对，他长得像保罗·纽曼。

118
00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:29.280
He has a side hustle of selling mixed salad dressings
他的副业是在跳蚤市场

119
00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.680
at a flea market for a loss.
亏本出售混合沙拉酱。

120
00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:31.040
What?
什么？

121
00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:36.640
I mean, lady, Paul Newman is known for his blue eyes.
我的意思是，女士，保罗·纽曼可是以他的蓝眼睛闻名的。

122
00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:37.840
Piercing blue.
深邃的蓝色。

123
00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:41.220
Yeah, I mean, Steve has like hazely eyes.
对，我的意思是，史蒂夫的眼睛有点像榛色。

124
00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.200
He has nice eyes.
他的眼睛很好看。

125
00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:43.580
Sometimes they look green.
有时候看起来是绿色的。

126
00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.240
Sometimes they look brown to me.
在我看来有时候又是棕色的。

127
00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:45.760
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

128
00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:47.940
They're not Paul Newman's eyes.
那可不是保罗·纽曼的眼睛。

129
00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:49.720
Well, don't tell Michael that.
好吧，别跟迈克尔这么说。

130
00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.620
But I feel like that's so true.
不过我觉得这太真实了。

131
00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:53.960
You know, everyone has a friend
你知道的，每个人都有一个朋友

132
00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.980
who thinks they look like someone really famous
他觉得自己长得像某个超级大明星

133
00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.780
and you're like, I don't see it.
然后你会想：我真的一点也看不出来。

134
00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:00.620
I mean, it's so reminding me of the love is blind
我的意思是，这太让我想起《爱情盲选》了

135
00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:04.740
and the poor woman who said that people tell her
还有那个可怜的女人，她说别人告诉她

136
00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:06.320
that she looks like Megan Fox
她长得像梅根·福克斯

137
00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:09.160
and like the guy on the other side of the wall
然后墙另一边的那个家伙

138
00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.000
is like loses his mind.
简直快要失去理智了。

139
00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:15.320
Like he can never think of dating anyone else in the pods
就好像他再也不想跟小黑屋里的任何人约会了

140
00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:19.420
because he thinks he's going to leave with Megan Fox.
因为他觉得自己能带走梅根·福克斯。

141
00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:23.920
I mean, I get some of the resemblance,
我的意思是，我能看出一点相似之处

142
00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:28.620
but I mean, I don't know what the comparison would be,
但我的意思是，我不知道该怎么比喻

143
00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:31.740
but I mean, it's just like, it's a big leap.
不过我的意思是，这感觉就像是个巨大的跨越。

144
00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:32.600
Okay.
好吧。

145
00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.560
I mean, like you want to be accurate,
我的意思是，你希望准确一点

146
00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.060
especially when you're like dating,
特别是当你像在约会时

147
00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:40.080
like in the pods.
比如在小黑屋里的时候。

148
00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:40.880
I mean.
我是说。

149
00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:42.960
But like, I mean, this guy's eyes,
但比如说，这家伙的眼睛

150
00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:45.060
like they like literally like a cartoon.
简直就像漫画里的一样。

151
00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:48.020
They're like, but going like he can't like believe
他们就好像，就好像他简直不敢相信

152
00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:51.200
that he's about to hook up with Megan Fox.
他居然要和梅根·福克斯在一起了。

153
00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:53.840
Well, you know what I want to see?
好吧，你知道我想看什么吗？

154
00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.400
Michael Scott on Love is Blind.
迈克尔·斯科特上《盲约》。

155
00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:57.960
Oh my God.
噢，天哪。

156
00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.180
Yes, please.
太好了，求之不得。

157
00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:02.580
You know, there's a whole new season of Love is Blind
你知道，有一整季全新的《盲约》

158
00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:03.800
that was just on,
刚刚播出，

159
00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.280
but I haven't watched it yet.
但我还没看。

160
00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:06.080
I was in Chicago.
我当时在芝加哥。

161
00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:07.780
Should I finally watch it?
我是不是该终于去看看了？

162
00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:08.640
Should we watch it?
我们要不要看？

163
00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:10.700
I mean, maybe, I don't know.
我的意思是，也许吧，我不知道。

164
00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.500
Like the reunion has aired
就像大结局重聚特辑已经播出了

165
00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:16.520
and I'm seeing all like the funny recreation videos
而我在Instagram上

166
00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:17.260
on Instagram.
看到了各种搞笑的模仿视频。

167
00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.840
I don't know any of the references.
我完全不懂这些梗。

168
